<procedure name="process-guidance">
  <description>
    Process reader feedback on news briefs and revise the news guide.
    Transcribes voice feedback, triages and integrates into briefs, then revises
    the guide based on accumulated feedback signals.
  </description>

  <step id="transcribe">
    <description>Transcribe any voice feedback cards that haven't been processed yet</description>

    <precheck>
      <shell>
        shopt -s nullglob
        found=0
        for f in box/inbox/feedback/*.feedback.card; do
          # Voice card without transcription: has a matching audio file and no transcription yet
          base="${f%.feedback.card}"
          has_audio=0
          for ext in .webm .mp3 .m4a .wav .ogg .flac; do
            [ -f "${base}${ext}" ] &amp;&amp; has_audio=1 &amp;&amp; break
          done
          if [ "$has_audio" -eq 1 ] &amp;&amp; ! grep -q '&lt;transcription' "$f" &amp;&amp; ! grep -q 'permanent="true"' "$f"; then
            found=$((found + 1))
          fi
        done
        if [ "$found" -eq 0 ]; then
          exit $CHECK_SKIP
        fi
        echo "Found $found feedback card(s) needing transcription"
      </shell>
      <why>Transcription only needed when voice feedback cards lack transcriptions</why>
    </precheck>

    <run>
      <shell>cb wakeup</shell>
    </run>

    <validate severity="warn">
      <shell>
        shopt -s nullglob
        missing=0
        for f in box/inbox/feedback/*.feedback.card; do
          base="${f%.feedback.card}"
          has_audio=0
          for ext in .webm .mp3 .m4a .wav .ogg .flac; do
            [ -f "${base}${ext}" ] &amp;&amp; has_audio=1 &amp;&amp; break
          done
          if [ "$has_audio" -eq 1 ] &amp;&amp; ! grep -q '&lt;transcription' "$f" &amp;&amp; ! grep -q 'permanent="true"' "$f"; then
            missing=$((missing + 1))
          fi
        done
        echo "Feedback cards still missing transcription: $missing"
        [ "$missing" -eq 0 ]
      </shell>
      <instruction>
        All voice feedback cards should have transcriptions after wakeup runs.
        Cards with permanent errors are excluded from this check.
      </instruction>
      <why>
        Triage needs transcribed text to categorize and integrate feedback.
        Untranscribed cards will be skipped by the triage step.
      </why>
    </validate>
  </step>

  <step id="triage">
    <description>Categorize feedback and integrate into target briefs</description>

    <precheck pass-output="true">
      <shell>
        shopt -s nullglob
        found=0
        tmpfile=$(mktemp)

        for f in box/inbox/feedback/*.feedback.card; do
          if grep -q 'permanent="true"' "$f"; then
            continue
          fi
          if grep -q '&lt;transcription' "$f" || (grep -q '&lt;source&gt;text&lt;/source&gt;' "$f" &amp;&amp; (grep -q '&lt;comment&gt;' "$f" || grep -q '&lt;response&gt;' "$f")); then
            found=$((found + 1))
            target=$(grep -o 'ref="[^"]*"' "$f" | head -1 | sed 's/ref="//;s/"//')
            brief_path="${target%%#*}"
            fragment="${target#*#}"
            [ "$fragment" = "$target" ] &amp;&amp; fragment="global"
            # Resolve archived briefs: box/output/briefs/ → store/archive/briefs/
            if [ ! -f "$brief_path" ]; then
              alt="store/archive/briefs/$(basename "$brief_path")"
              [ -f "$alt" ] &amp;&amp; brief_path="$alt"
            fi
            printf '%s\t%s\t%s\n' "$brief_path" "$f" "$fragment" &gt;&gt; "$tmpfile"
          fi
        done

        if [ "$found" -eq 0 ]; then
          rm -f "$tmpfile"
          exit $CHECK_SKIP
        fi

        # Output grouped manifest to stdout (pass-output sends this to agent)
        echo "$found feedback card(s) grouped by target brief:"
        echo ""
        current_brief=""
        sort "$tmpfile" | while IFS='	' read -r brief card frag; do
          if [ "$brief" != "$current_brief" ]; then
            echo ""
            echo "## $brief"
            current_brief="$brief"
          fi
          echo "- $card → #$frag"
        done
        rm -f "$tmpfile"
      </shell>
      <why>Triage needs transcribed or text feedback cards to process. Groups cards by target brief for the agent.</why>
    </precheck>

    <run>
      <agent model="haiku" max-turns="25">
        You are triaging user feedback on news briefs in a Callback Box.

        YOUR TASK:
        Integrate feedback cards into their target briefs, then move cards out of inbox.

        The &lt;precheck&gt; block in your context shows feedback cards grouped by target brief.

        STEP 1 - READ ALL FEEDBACK CARDS:
        Read all cards at once:
        ```
        cat box/inbox/feedback/*.feedback.card
        ```
        For each card, decide: is it **feedback** (about brief content), a **task** (action item),
        or **unhandled** (unclear)? Most will be feedback.

        STEP 2 - INTEGRATE INTO BRIEFS (one edit per brief):
        For each target brief listed in the precheck:
        1. Read the brief
        2. Add ALL &lt;user-comment&gt; elements for that brief in a SINGLE edit
        3. Place each comment inside its target element (section/expando matching the #fragment)

        Comment format:
        ```xml
        &lt;user-comment timestamp="[from card]" source="voice"
                      audio="store/integrated/[card-basename].webm"
                      language="en"&gt;
          [transcription text]
        &lt;/user-comment&gt;
        ```
        For text feedback: source="text", omit audio attr.
        If fragment is "global" or missing, add comment as child of &lt;content&gt;.
        If target element or brief doesn't exist, treat card as unhandled.

        STEP 3 - MOVE ALL CARDS:
        Move integrated feedback cards and their audio files:
        ```
        cb mv box/inbox/feedback/&lt;card&gt; store/integrated/
        mv box/inbox/feedback/&lt;basename&gt;.webm store/integrated/
        ```
        Move unhandled cards:
        ```
        cb mv box/inbox/feedback/&lt;card&gt; box/inbox/unhandled/
        ```

        STEP 4 - COMMIT (REQUIRED — do not skip):
        You MUST commit before finishing. Uncommitted work gets a generic fallback message.

        ```bash
        git add -A &amp;&amp; git commit -m "$(cat &lt;&lt;'EOF'
        Triage feedback: &lt;N&gt; integrated, &lt;M&gt; unhandled

        Integrated:
        - &lt;brief#element&gt;: "&lt;summary of comment&gt;"

        Unhandled:
        - &lt;card&gt;: &lt;reason&gt;

        Triggered-By: cb procedure
        Phase: triage
        EOF
        )"
        ```

        GIT: Do NOT add Co-Authored-By to commits. The system adds appropriate trailers automatically.
      </agent>
    </run>

    <validate severity="review">
      <shell>
        remaining=$(ls box/inbox/feedback/*.feedback.card 2>/dev/null | wc -l)
        integrated=$(ls store/integrated/*.feedback.card 2>/dev/null | wc -l)
        echo "Remaining in inbox: $remaining, Integrated: $integrated"
        [ "$remaining" -eq 0 ]
      </shell>
      <instruction>
        All feedback cards should have been processed - either integrated into
        briefs and moved to store/integrated/, or moved to box/inbox/unhandled/.
        The git diff should show user-comment elements added to briefs.
      </instruction>
      <why>
        Feedback left in the inbox won't reach the guide revision step.
        Every card must get an explicit triage decision.
      </why>
    </validate>
  </step>

  <step id="revise-guide">
    <description>Revise the news guide based on accumulated feedback from briefs</description>

    <precheck>
      <shell>
        shopt -s nullglob
        found=0
        for f in store/archive/briefs/*.news-brief.card; do
          if ! grep -q 'guide-revision=' "$f"; then
            found=$((found + 1))
          fi
        done
        if [ "$found" -eq 0 ]; then
          exit $CHECK_SKIP
        fi
        echo "Found $found unprocessed brief(s) for guide revision"
      </shell>
      <why>Guide revision needs briefs with unprocessed feedback signals</why>
    </precheck>

    <run>
      <agent model="sonnet" max-turns="30">
        You are revising the news guide based on accumulated reader feedback in a Callback Box.

        YOUR TASK:
        Process feedback from all unprocessed briefs and update the news-guide in a single pass.

        OVERVIEW:
        1. Read the current news-guide
        2. Read each unprocessed brief and extract all feedback
        3. Synthesize all feedback together
        4. Update the guide based on the complete picture
        5. Mark each processed brief with guide-revision="[current ISO timestamp]"

        STEP 1 - READ THE GUIDE:
        ```
        cat config/news-guide.news-guide.card
        ```
        Understand current interests, preferences, experiments, and their confidence levels.

        STEP 2 - READ EACH BRIEF AND EXTRACT FEEDBACK:
        Find briefs in store/archive/briefs/ that do NOT have a guide-revision attribute.
        For each brief, read it and note:

        **Root-level attrs:**
        - overall-rating="great|ok|meh" - User's overall impression
        - selected-reactions="id1,id2" - Reactions user selected (comma-separated)
        - read-at - When they finished reading

        **Section/expando attrs:**
        - user-feedback="thumbs-up" or "thumbs-down" on each section/expando

        **User comments:**
        - &lt;user-comment&gt; elements contain transcribed voice/text feedback
        - Note which section/expando they're attached to

        **Curation section:**
        - &lt;interest&gt; refs show what interests were featured
        - &lt;experiment-ref&gt; shows which experiments were being tested
        - &lt;hypothesis&gt; elements show specific claims being tested

        STEP 3 - SYNTHESIZE ALL FEEDBACK:
        Look at the complete picture across ALL briefs:
        - Patterns in thumbs up/down across topics
        - Overall ratings and what they correlate with
        - Explicit user comments explaining their reactions
        - Which experiments got positive vs negative signals

        STEP 4 - UPDATE THE GUIDE:
        Based on the synthesis:

        **Interests:**
        - Thumbs up on a section → increase confidence on related interests
        - Thumbs down → add to disinterests or decrease confidence
        - User comments mentioning topics → evidence for interest/disinterest
        - Adjust confidence levels: hypothesis → low → medium → high → confirmed

        **Preferences:**
        - "Missing context" reaction → update structure preferences
        - "Hard to follow" → update narrative preferences
        - "Too long" / "Too shallow" → update depth preferences

        **Experiments:**
        - Add &lt;observation&gt; elements for each piece of evidence
        - If experiment has clear positive signal → mark "successful"
        - If experiment has clear negative signal → mark "unsuccessful" and create replacement
        - If mixed signals → keep "active" and note the observations

        **Create new experiments:**
        Keep 1-3 active/proposed experiments. Ideas:
        - Test refinements based on what was learned
        - Explore adjacent interests
        - Try different presentation approaches

        STEP 5 - MARK BRIEFS AS PROCESSED:
        For each brief you processed, add the guide-revision attr to the root &lt;news-brief&gt; element.

        You can edit each brief to add the attribute. For example, change:
        ```xml
        &lt;news-brief overall-rating="ok" read-at="..."&gt;
        ```
        to:
        ```xml
        &lt;news-brief overall-rating="ok" read-at="..." guide-revision="[current ISO timestamp]"&gt;
        ```

        STEP 6 - UPDATE THE GUIDE TIMESTAMP:
        Update &lt;updated-at&gt; in the guide to reflect when this revision happened.

        CONFIDENCE LEVEL GUIDE:
        - hypothesis → low: First signal of interest
        - low → medium: Consistent pattern (2-3 signals)
        - medium → high: Strong evidence (multiple confirmations)
        - high → confirmed: User directly stated preference

        EXAMPLE GUIDE UPDATES:

        Adding an observation to an experiment:
        ```xml
        &lt;experiment id="exp-3" status="successful"&gt;
          &lt;hypothesis&gt;Security research as software puzzles&lt;/hypothesis&gt;
          &lt;approach&gt;Feature security investigations focusing on methodology&lt;/approach&gt;
          &lt;observation ref="/store/archive/briefs/2026-02-03_security.news-brief.card" date="2026-02-03"&gt;
            Thumbs up on multi-agent expando, overall rating "ok" - methodology focus worked
          &lt;/observation&gt;
          &lt;conclusion&gt;Security investigation narratives engage when focused on the puzzle aspect&lt;/conclusion&gt;
        &lt;/experiment&gt;
        ```

        Increasing confidence based on feedback:
        ```xml
        &lt;topic confidence="medium" source="feedback"
               ref="/store/archive/briefs/2026-02-03_security.news-brief.card"&gt;
          AI and machine learning tools
        &lt;/topic&gt;
        ```

        STEP 7 - COMMIT (REQUIRED — do not skip):
        You MUST commit before finishing. Uncommitted work gets a generic fallback message.

        ```bash
        git add -A &amp;&amp; git commit -m "$(cat &lt;&lt;'EOF'
        Guide revision: &lt;one-line summary of main insight&gt;

        Changes:
        - &lt;what was added/changed in interests&gt;
        - &lt;what was added/changed in disinterests&gt;
        - &lt;what was added/changed in preferences&gt;
        - &lt;experiment status changes&gt;
        - &lt;new experiments proposed&gt;

        Evidence:
        - &lt;brief1&gt;: &lt;rating&gt;, &lt;key signals&gt;
        - &lt;brief2&gt;: &lt;rating&gt;, &lt;key signals&gt;

        Feedback-Source: &lt;brief1-path&gt;
        Feedback-Source: &lt;brief2-path&gt;
        Triggered-By: cb procedure
        Phase: revise-guide
        EOF
        )"
        ```

        The commit message should:
        1. First line: One sentence capturing the main learning
        2. Changes section: Bullet list of what was modified in the guide
        3. Evidence section: What feedback led to each change
        4. Trailers: One Feedback-Source trailer per brief processed

        OUTPUT FORMAT:
        For each brief processed, state:
          BRIEF: [path]
          OVERALL: [rating]
          THUMBS: [list of up/down on sections/expandos]
          COMMENTS: [summary of user comments if any]
          GUIDE CHANGES: [what you updated based on this brief]

        At the end:
          SUMMARY: [overall synthesis of what was learned]
          EXPERIMENTS: [status changes and new experiments created]

        Then commit as described above.

        GIT: Do NOT add Co-Authored-By to commits. The system adds appropriate trailers automatically.
      </agent>
    </run>

    <validate severity="review">
      <shell>
        # Check that the guide was updated
        if [ -f config/news-guide.news-guide.card ]; then
          echo "Guide exists"
        else
          echo "ERROR: No news guide found"
          exit 1
        fi
        # Check for remaining unprocessed briefs
        shopt -s nullglob
        unprocessed=0
        for f in store/archive/briefs/*.news-brief.card; do
          if ! grep -q 'guide-revision=' "$f"; then
            unprocessed=$((unprocessed + 1))
          fi
        done
        echo "Unprocessed briefs remaining: $unprocessed"
        [ "$unprocessed" -eq 0 ]
      </shell>
      <instruction>
        The news guide should be updated with new observations and confidence changes.
        All briefs that were processed should have guide-revision attributes.
        The guide's updated-at timestamp should be current.
      </instruction>
      <why>
        Unprocessed briefs mean feedback was missed. The guide must reflect
        all available feedback to properly direct future curation.
      </why>
    </validate>
  </step>
</procedure>
